<title>UK: Seton buys sleep aid product from SmithKline.</title>
<headline>Seton buys sleep aid product from SmithKline.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seton Healthcare Group Plc said on Friday that it has bought a sleep aid product called Sominex from SmithKline Beecham Plc for 800,000 pounds.</p>
<p>The payment will be made in September 1997.</p>
<p>Seton chief executive Iain Cater said, &quot;Sominex represents another good addition to our OTC range of products and complements our existing portfolio of brands.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
